IMPORT prelude
-- THE CAST WORD AND AN UNKNOWN ROLL ENTRY (smucclaw/l4-ide#998).
--
-- `EVERY Tenant t IN roll` drops a roll entry that the constructor `Tenant`
-- did not build. An entry whose value is not known may or may not be a
-- tenant, so dropping it would answer for it: the join would then release
-- without that member's obligation, which is how this used to report
-- FULFILLED. Now it is Stuck, naming the unknown, which is what the same
-- roll gives with no cast word at all.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"

§ `Facts`
    GIVEN u IS AN Actor

-- 1. The roll holds an unknown. Alice signs; whether `u` must sign too
--    depends on what `u` is, so this is Stuck on `u`.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`roll with unknown` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN LIST alice, u
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `roll with unknown` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1

-- 2. Control: the second entry is a known tenant. Bob has not signed, so his
--    obligation is still pending.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`roll with bob` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN LIST alice, bob
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `roll with bob` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1

-- 3. Control: no cast word. The unknown is admitted, and the run is Stuck on
--    it as soon as its obligation is checked against Alice's signature.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`roll uncast` MEANS
    EVERY t IN LIST alice, u
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `roll uncast` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1

-- 4. Control: an entry KNOWN to be built by another constructor is still left
--    out. The landlord is not a tenant, so Alice's signature is enough.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`roll with landlord` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN LIST alice, theLandlord
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   BREACH

#TRACE `roll with landlord` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
